BT 1 0 0 1 0 62 Tm /F2 10.5 Tf 14.5 TL .657392 Tw (Low-code platforms allow applications to be developed mainly through visual development tools instead of) Tj T* 0 Tw .325424 Tw (writing large amounts of traditional program code. Applications are assembled using predefined components) Tj T* 0 Tw .300685 Tw (such as forms, reports and dashboards, and behaviour is defined through workflows, rules and configuration.) Tj T* 0 Tw .357639 Tw (A small amount of scripting is usually available for specific needs. This approach reduces development time) Tj T* 0 Tw (and effort and makes it possible for a wider range of people to take part in building business applications.) Tj T* ET
